    <!-- ==========================================
         TOPIC DEFINITIONS
    =========================================== -->

    <h4>

        📖 Topic Definitions

    </h4>


    <div class="accordion"
         id="percentageTopics">


        <!-- ======================================
             BASIC PERCENTAGE
        ======================================= -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#basicPercentage">

                    1. Basic Percentage

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="basicPercentage"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Percentage represents a quantity out of 100.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Formula:</strong>

                    <br>

                    Percentage =
                    (Value ÷ Total) × 100

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Example:</strong>

                    <br>

                    If a student scores 40 marks out of 50:

                    <br><br>

                    Percentage =
                    (40 ÷ 50) × 100 = 80%

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- ======================================
             PERCENTAGE INCREASE
        ======================================= -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#percentageIncrease">

                    2. Percentage Increase

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="percentageIncrease"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Percentage increase shows how much a value
                    has increased compared with its original value.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Formula:</strong>

                    <br>

                    Percentage Increase =
                    (Increase ÷ Original Value) × 100

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Example:</strong>

                    <br>

                    A salary increases from ₹20,000 to ₹25,000.

                    <br><br>

                    Increase = ₹5,000

                    <br>

                    Percentage Increase =
                    (5,000 ÷ 20,000) × 100 = 25%

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- ======================================
             PERCENTAGE DECREASE
        ======================================= -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#percentageDecrease">

                    3. Percentage Decrease

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="percentageDecrease"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Percentage decrease shows how much a value
                    has decreased compared with its original value.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Formula:</strong>

                    <br>

                    Percentage Decrease =
                    (Decrease ÷ Original Value) × 100

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Example:</strong>

                    <br>

                    A price decreases from ₹500 to ₹400.

                    <br><br>

                    Decrease = ₹100

                    <br>

                    Percentage Decrease =
                    (100 ÷ 500) × 100 = 20%

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- ======================================
             SUCCESSIVE PERCENTAGE
        ======================================= -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#successivePercentage">

                    4. Successive Percentage

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="successivePercentage"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Successive percentage means applying two or
                    more percentage changes one after another.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Formula for two increases:</strong>

                    <br>

                    Net Increase =
                    A + B + (AB ÷ 100)

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Example:</strong>

                    <br>

                    A value increases by 10% and then by 20%.

                    <br>

                    Net increase =
                    10 + 20 + (10 × 20 ÷ 100)

                    = 32%

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- ======================================
             MARKS PERCENTAGE
        ======================================= -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#marksPercentage">

                    5. Marks Percentage

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="marksPercentage"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Marks percentage represents the marks
                    obtained compared with the total marks.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Formula:</strong>

                    <br>

                    Percentage =
                    (Marks Obtained ÷ Total Marks) × 100

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Example:</strong>

                    <br>

                    A student scores 450 out of 500.

                    <br><br>

                    Percentage =
                    (450 ÷ 500) × 100 = 90%

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- ======================================
             POPULATION PERCENTAGE
        ======================================= -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#populationPercentage">

                    6. Population Percentage

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="populationPercentage"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Population percentage is used to calculate
                    the increase or decrease in population.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Example:</strong>

                    <br>

                    If a city's population is 1,00,000 and
                    increases by 10%, the new population is:

                    <br><br>

                    1,00,000 + 10% of 1,00,000

                    <br>

                    = 1,10,000

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- ======================================
             SALARY PERCENTAGE
        ======================================= -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#salaryPercentage">

                    7. Salary Percentage

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="salaryPercentage"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Percentage calculations are commonly used
                    to calculate salary hikes, deductions,
                    bonuses and changes in income.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Example:</strong>

                    <br>

                    If a salary of ₹40,000 increases by 15%:

                    <br><br>

                    Increase =
                    15% of ₹40,000 = ₹6,000

                    <br>

                    New salary = ₹46,000

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


    </div>


